  "title": "Correctness of the sampler initialization program",
  "preamble": "import Definitions.Def_ExpandingCodes_PolynomialStretch_BinaryRuntime\n\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nopen scoped Classical\nopen NKtLB\n",
  "formal_statement": "theorem ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.prelude_stops {R : ℕ} (r : Fin 80 → Fin R) (hr : Function.Injective r)\n    (d n k : ℕ) (hd : 1 ≤ d) (hk : 0<k) (hn : 2 ≤ n) (hnk : k ≤ n)\n    (inp : Inputs) (hi : inp.input=ExpandingCodes.PolynomialStretch.sizeInput n) (M : ℕ) (hM : ExpandingCodes.PolynomialStretch.SamplerEnvelopeCovers d k n M) :\n    ∃ t e,t ≤ ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.preludeTime d n M ∧\n      (ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.samplerFrontendProgram r hr d k).Stops inp ((ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.initialStore R 2).toCfg (ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.samplerFrontendProgram r hr d k).entry) t e ∧\n      e.store=ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.preludeStore r hr d n k inp ∧ ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.RuntimeReady r d n k inp M e.store ∧ e.output=[] := by sorry\n",
  "natural_statement": "Given the unary size input and a valid polynomial envelope, the sampler initialization tape program produces its specified runtime-ready store within the stated time bound and with empty output.",
  "source": "Algorithmic supporting lemma for Section 2 of Isaac M Hair and Amit Sahai, Expanding Codes with Polynomial Stretch; the explicit tape-machine implementation is formalized in ExpandingCodes.Computation.SamplerAssembly.",
  "proof_route": "The proof composes parameter setup, random-table generation, canonical field setup, and storage initialization; each phase contributes a separately bounded execution.",
